# Weakens R's StraddlerBelowInit in this module's environment: a straddler of the
# purged incarnation is allocated after the re-created incarnation's first
# initialisation recorded its heads, above them. The re-created incarnation's live
# advance passes it. Shows the assumption is load-bearing.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestAssumeStraddlerAfterInit
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a straddler is allocated whether or not the re-created incarnation has initialised
PERTURBS: StraddlerAlloc
BOUNDS: WithRecreate = TRUE, WithUnclaimedSurvivor = FALSE, WithPreArm = FALSE

--- FIND
    /\ recreated
    /\ ~reinit
    /\ ~spUsed
--- REPLACE
    /\ recreated
\* MUTATION: allocated after the initialisation's heads too.
    /\ ~spUsed
--- END
